                       Dice for Teleconference
                   for The Major BBS v10 - version 1.0.0

              Copyright (c) 2026 Elwynor Technologies.
   Originally HOTELeconference Dice by Randall R. Spangler, annex.com.
     Dice converted for The Major BBS v10 by Mark Laudenbach -
                    https://github.com/laudenbachm


WHAT IT DOES
------------

Dice rolling for the stock Teleconference.  In any channel, type

     DICE ON
     ROLL 3D8

You see your roll in color.  Everyone else in the channel sees one line
of chat from you, such as

     From Mark: [Dice] rolls 3 8-sided dice and gets 5, 2 and 7 (for a
     total of 14).

Because the roll is sent as ordinary chat, it also reaches users on
other boards in a linked channel, such as MajorLink.  Those boards don't
need Dice installed.


COMMANDS
--------

     DICE ON          allow you to roll dice (ROLL does nothing until then,
                      unless the Sysop has set it to start on)
     DICE OFF         turn dice rolling off again
     DICE HELP        show help
     ROLL D20         roll one 20-sided die
     ROLL 3D8         roll three 8-sided dice
     ROLL 4           roll four 6-sided dice
     ROLL OFF         same as DICE OFF

Spaces and capitals don't matter.  The Sysop sets how many dice can be
rolled at once (up to 100) and the most sides a die can have (up to
1000); the defaults are 50 and 100.


FOR THE SYSOP
-------------

Install ELWDCTEL.DLL, ELWDCTEL.MDF, ELWDCTEL.MSG and ELWDCTEL.RLN, add
the module in the Major BBS configuration, and restart the board.  The
Teleconference (GALTELE) must be installed.  Dice adds its commands when
the board starts, whatever order the modules load in.

Settings are changed online, with no restart: in Teleconference, a user
with the SYSOP key types

     DICE SET                    list the settings
     DICE SET <number> <value>   change one
     DICE SET DEFAULTS           put everything back

You can turn dice off, choose a key users need, limit dice to certain
channels, and set the dice and sides limits.  Every change is written
to the Audit Trail.

The wording of every message is in ELWDCTEL.MSG.  The lines that begin
PUB are what the rest of the channel sees; keep them to one plain line,
since boards on the other end of a link may not show colors the way yours
does.

Note: copying a new ELWDCTEL.MSG over the old one replaces any text you
changed in it.


VERSION HISTORY
---------------

1.0.0 (27 October 2026)

  First release for The Major BBS v10, converted from HOTELeconference
  Dice 2.00 (1997).
  - Works in the stock Teleconference, including linked channels such
    as MajorLink.
  - Online settings (DICE SET) instead of configuration editor options.
  - Choose which channels the dice work in.
  - Fixed: a user without the required key could get an undefined
    result from the DICE command.
  - Fixed: extra characters after a roll ("3D8x") are now refused
    instead of silently ignored.
  - Rolls use the operating system's random number generator.
